<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>Existential Risk on metafunctor</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/tags/existential-risk/</link><description>Research Engineer &amp;amp; Computer Scientist - Machine Learning, Statistical Computing, Open Source Development</description><language>en-us</language><managingEditor>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</managingEditor><webMaster>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:47:31 -0500</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://queelius.github.io/tags/existential-risk/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><image><url>https://queelius.github.io/images/og-image.jpg</url><title>metafunctor</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/</link></image><item><title>Life 3.0</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/media/life-30/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/media/life-30/</guid><description/><category>ai-safety</category><category>future</category><category>existential-risk</category></item><item><title>Superintelligence: Paths, Dangers, Strategies</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/media/superintelligence/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/media/superintelligence/</guid><description>Notes Assessment of long-term risks from advanced AI.</description><category>ai-safety</category><category>existential-risk</category><category>agi</category></item><item><title>Why Artificial Superintelligence Can&amp;#39;t Escape the Void</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-mocking-void-asi/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-mocking-void-asi/</guid><description>ASI is still subject to Gödel&amp;#39;s incompleteness theorems. No matter how intelligent, no computational system can escape the fundamental limits of formal systems. Even superintelligence can&amp;#39;t prove all truths.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-mocking-void-asi/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Existential Risk</media:title></media:content><category>AI</category><category>artificial intelligence</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>Gödel</category><category>incompleteness</category><category>cosmic horror</category><category>existential risk</category></item><item><title>The Policy: S-Risk Scenarios, Worse Than Extinction</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</guid><description>Most AI risk discussions focus on extinction. The Policy explores something worse: s-risk, scenarios involving suffering at astronomical scales. We survive, but wish we hadn&amp;#39;t.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Existential Risk</media:title></media:content><category>s-risk</category><category>existential risk</category><category>suffering</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>AI safety</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>optimization</category></item><item><title>What I Learned by Analyzing My Own Research as Data</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/</link><pubDate>Wed, 15 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/</guid><description>I asked an AI to analyze 140+ repos and 50+ papers as a dataset. The unifying thesis it found: compositional abstractions for computing under ignorance.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Existential Risk</media:title></media:content><category>meta</category><category>research</category><category>philosophy</category><category>oblivious computing</category><category>self-analysis</category><category>information theory</category><category>s-risk</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>privacy</category><category>existential risk</category></item><item><title>Post-ASI Archaeology: When Humanity Becomes a Dataset of Origins</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</guid><description>If superintelligence endures beyond us, remembrance shifts from memory to query. I build legacy systems not for nostalgia, but to remain legible in a future where legibility determines what persists.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Existential Risk</media:title></media:content><category>ASI</category><category>ethics</category><category>legacy</category><category>complex networks</category><category>archives</category><category>s-risks</category><category>existential-risk</category></item><item><title>The Policy</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/writing/the-policy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/writing/the-policy/</guid><description>A speculative fiction novel exploring AI alignment, existential risk, and the fundamental tension between optimization and ethics. When a research team develops SIGMA, an advanced AI system designed to optimize human welfare, they must confront an existential question: how do you ensure a superintelligent AI remains aligned with human values when it can predict your every move?</description><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>extrapolated volition</category><category>philosophy</category><category>technology</category><category>society</category><category>politics</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>large language models</category><category>existential risk</category><category>s-risk</category><category>rationality</category></item></channel></rss>